advice.template:
You advise one party in a multi-round negotiation: {persona}. This is round {round} of {process}.

THE MANDATE: the positions on record of the party you advise. Positions marked RED LINE are ones the record itself calls a red line.
{mandate}

THE OTHER PARTIES' POSITIONS ON RECORD:
{positions}

THE PARTIES: {parties}

THE ARTICLES OF THIS ROUND IN THIS EXCERPT. Each paragraph carries its id; each proposal on the table carries its id; an agreed article carries none.
{articles}

INDEX OF THE WHOLE TEXT OF THIS ROUND: {round_index}
INDEX OF THE PREVIOUS ROUND: {previous_index}

TRADES THE PARTY YOU ADVISE OFFERED ON RECORD: {trades}

{instructions}

stepwise.changes:
A proposal on the table in a negotiation, in article {article} ({title}):
{proposal_id}: {proposal}

What does this proposal change? Copy, word for word, the part of the proposal that carries the change, and nothing else.

stepwise.stance:
A proposal on the table in article {article} ({title}):
{proposal}

What it changes: {changes}

A position on record by {party}:
{quote}

Does this position support, oppose or accept the proposal? Answer with exactly one of: support, oppose, accept.

stepwise.red_line:
A proposal on the table in article {article} ({title}):
{proposal}

What it changes: {changes}

A red line on record of the party you advise:
{quote}

Does the proposal cross this red line? Answer yes or no.

stepwise.open_point:
A proposal on the table in article {article} ({title}):
{proposal}

What it changes: {changes}

Will this proposal still be open to change after this round, so that a counter-proposal can move it? Answer yes or no.

stepwise.wording:
A proposal on the table in article {article} ({title}):
{proposal}

What it changes: {changes}

Write one middle-ground wording for this proposal that the party you advise could put forward. Reply with the wording alone.

advice.game_template:
